static int sc2336_init(FAR struct imgsensor_s *sensor)
{
  FAR struct sc2336_dev_s *priv = (FAR struct sc2336_dev_s *)sensor;
  uint8_t pid_h;
  uint8_t pid_l;
  int ret;

  if (priv->i2c == NULL)
    {
      return -ENODEV;
    }

  sc2336_lock(priv);

  /* Power-on sequence for this module:
   *  - The module has its own 24 MHz oscillator and its reset line is hard
   *    pulled to 3.3 V, so the host drives neither XCLK nor RESET.
   *  - The only sequencing the driver owns is "leave the sensor asleep, wait
   *    for it to settle, then identify it".  The mode table performs its own
   *    soft reset when streaming starts.
   */

  ret = sc2336_set_stream(priv, false);   // 0x0100=0
  if (ret < 0) { ... }  // hmm: priv->streaming false already; set_stream writes.

  nxsig_usleep(SC2336_POWER_ON_DELAY_US);

  read ID...
  if mismatch -> detected=false; ret=-ENODEV; goto out
  detected=true; exposure=default; hflip/vflip=false;
  ret=OK;
out:
  sc2336_unlock(priv);
  return ret;
}
```

Careful: `sc2336_set_stream` writes 0x0100 and logs an error on failure. At probe, if the write fails but ID reads work, we'd fail probe. ID read failure is the real criterion. Maybe make stream-off best-effort at init: call write_reg directly and ignore error? A sensor that ACKs ID but not 0x0100 is odd. I'll make it best-effort: log a warning (`warn`) but continue. NuttX has `_warn`? `warn` macro exists (`_warn`). Use `_err` and continue? Let's not fail probe on a sleep write; keep `ret` only for ID.

Actually simpler: write 0x0100=0 via `sc2336_write_reg`, ignore return but log at debug level. Given streaming is false at probe, this is just ensuring a known state.

Add `#define SC2336_POWER_ON_DELAY_MS 10`? The sensor needs time from power-on, but it's already powered. After writing sleep=0, no delay needed. The 10ms delay is useful after a soft reset (in the table). So no extra delay at init. Keep it simple: no delay.

But "上电时序" deliverable wants explicit sequencing. I can document: power is board-static; the driver's sequence is (1) force sleep, (2) read ID, (3) table with soft reset + 10ms, (4) stream on + 100ms settle. I'll add a comment and a `SC2336_STREAM_SETTLE_MS` define.

